        "topic": "Bank Reconciliation",
        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2014",
        "question_text": "<p>A cheque issued for $1,000 was recorded in the cash book as $100. What is the effect on the bank reconciliation statement?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The cash book balance is <b>understated</b> by $900 ($1,000 - $100). To reconcile, the cash book balance must be <b>increased by $900</b> to match the bank statement.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "82128",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Add $900 to the cash book balance",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "84058",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "Deduct $900 from the cash book balance",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "69746",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "Add $1,000 to the bank statement balance",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "68287",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "Deduct $100 from the bank statement balance",
                "is_correct": false
